         VALUES ('gQBXAAAAYAAJ', 'Weaveworld', array['Clive Barker'], 1997, 'Reissue of the highly acclaimed thriller by the world''s most outstanding dark fantasist. WEAVEWORLD is an epic adventure of the imagination. It begins with a carpet in which a world of rapture and enchantment is hiding; a world which comes to life, alerting the dark forces and beginning a desperate battle to preserve the last vestiges of magic which Humankind still has access to. WEAVEWORLD is a book of visions and horrors, a story of quest, titanic struggles, of love and of hope. It is a triumph of imagination and storytelling, an adventure, a nightmare, a promise... ''Barker''s fecundity of invention is beyond praise. In a world of hard-bitten horror and originality, Clive Barker dislocates your mind.'' THE MAIL ON SUNDAY.', 'https://books.google.com/books/content?id=gQBXAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&source=gbs_api', 760, 'http://play.google.com/books/reader?id=gQBXAAAAYAAJ&hl=&as_pt=BOOKS&source=gbs_api') ON CONFLICT (bookId) DO NOTHING;
